# Plugin Architecture

- Design for standard multi-harness plugin use: keep the core behavior in markdown files and avoid relying on harness-specific features unless there is a documented fallback.
- Keep repo-wide routing, orchestration, and default behavior in `CLAUDE.md`.
- Keep agent-specific usage guidance in `AGENTS.md`.
- Keep harness-specific compatibility notes and fallbacks in `docs/harness-compatibility.md`.
- When adding or removing plugin surface area, update `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` so skills, agents, commands, and hooks stay discoverable.
- Prefer patterns that degrade cleanly outside Claude Code. If a workflow depends on a Claude-specific tool or hook, document the manual or alternate path for other harnesses.
